  "label": "UK Government Policy Criticism",
  "description": "The meme is a form of political commentary that criticizes UK government policies, particularly gun control and media licensing. It uses the image of Queen Elizabeth II and Prince Charles — symbols of the British monarchy and state — to imply that the government is overreaching or absurd in its policies. This is a form of satire that relies on the public's perception of the monarchy as a symbol of national authority and tradition.",
